    "notes": [
      "Review: 130/130 checklist items by 8 reviewer(s) and a lead reviewer (showcase/runs/hardlift/0.1.0-rc.6/review-2).",
      "Review: 130/130 checklist items by 8 reviewers and the lead reviewer (showcase/runs/hardlift/0.1.0-rc.6/review-2). I opened the reference sheet, the blog home desktop-light sheet and the commerce cart desktop-dark sheet myself.",
      "Graded: the empty-cart sticker in dark mode stays minor. The coin and box still read as stickers, and the message and recovery button are fully readable. It is caused by the spec and shares a root with rc.6 review 1's dark sticker-fill minor. Both come from sticker colours following theme tokens. One fix covers both: sticker strokes, glyphs and fills keep the same colours in both themes.",
      "Merged: none needed across reviewers. Each finding breaks a different rule. The 'Loading…' text-only cards are separate from rc.6 review 1's pink busy-button minor (different element, different rule), and that earlier minor is not re-raised.",
      "Regressions against rc.5 critic-2 and rc.6 critic-1: none. Every rc.5 blocker and major is still fixed in all three samples. The save confirmation is an inline 'Saved' check that covers nothing. Hero stickers stay clear of the CTA (static below the text at phone width). Reflowed Revoke buttons keep their full size. The busy button keeps its fill and a readable label. Settings keeps one band colour across all its tabs in every sample.",
      "Family: the four apps read as one system in every sample. They share the paper-and-ink ground, regular-weight grotesk display type, one full-width band per section with an ink rule (the colour holds across a section's detail pages and tabs), ink current-page pills that turn paper in dark, outlined raised cards, the hard offset lift, pink price tags, a single pink action per view and the same dark mapping. Band colours rotate between samples (yellow, periwinkle, teal), as the spec allows.",
      "Recognition: someone who knows the reference would recognize it. The yellow or periwinkle hero carries tilted, edge-cropped pink coin stickers with an extruded rim, and one sample adds the linear tag wall. The shop is a dense wall of distinct flat, ink-outlined sticker products on band-colour squares with pink price tags. Pink pills are the loud accent, as on the reference.",
      "Signature elements hold across apps: section bands, outline pills, flat heavy-outlined sticker art (a different object per product, one sticker per empty state), the turning-coin loader (fully shown in 1 of 3 samples, in the busy button only in the others), the hard lift on whole cards and buttons, and the pink halo on focused inputs. The remaining weak spot is sticker colours in dark mode.",
      "Not re-raised (earlier minors): dark sticker fills on the blog; ghost busy button turning pink; bold titles in reflowed table blocks; the near-flush light focus ring beside the current-page pill; the ink Subscribe in the newsletter error state; Shop not marked current on product pages; the switch pink vs ink contradiction; the empty-filter sticker size; the leftover column-label strip on mobile tables.",
      "Verdict: passes. No blockers or majors. Nine minors, two caused by the spec: sticker stroke and glyph follow the theme in dark mode, and the pill recipe makes every aria-current pill ink, sub-nav included."
